# Navigate to the parent directory (W:\Java)
cd W:\Java

# Compile all files in the package
javac QuizApp\*.java

# Run using the full package name
java QuizApp.Main

--> Why This Works:

1. Java looks for packages relative to the current directory
2. When you're in Java and run javac QuizApp\*.java, Java understands that QuizApp is a package
3. When you run java QuizApp.Main, Java finds the QuizApp package in the current directory and locates the Main class within it

--> Key Points to Remember:

1. Never compile individual files when using packages - always compile all related files together
2. Always compile from the parent directory of your package structure
3. Use the full package name when running the program (e.g., QuizApp.Main, not just Main)